Refuse, on wasip1, the commands the Fastly CLI for slicc cannot run.

Reason: these commands need a native program, a local port, or a new fastly
binary, and would otherwise fail deep inside with ENOSYS or a missing
executable. On wasip1 they now stop first with a RemediationError that
says why and what to do instead:
- compute build and compute publish (and compute hash-files without
  --package, in BuildCommand): the language toolchain and wasm-tools;
  deploy a package built elsewhere with compute deploy --package;
- compute serve (Viceroy on a local port), compute init (git and post-init
  scripts), compute install-tools (downloads Viceroy);
- vcl serve (it publishes the VCL to a Fiddle sandbox, then listens on a
  local port);
- update and install (they replace the binary; the npm package is the
  update);
- SSO (auth login --sso, sso, profile create/update --sso): it waits for
  the browser's redirect to http://localhost:8080/callback, which a slicc
  command cannot receive; use FASTLY_API_TOKEN, auth add --api-token or
  auth login with a pasted token.
On wasip1 there is also no update check (it would ask Fastly for a wasip1
binary on every command), no build-data notice (no builds, and the notice
waits 5 seconds), and the SSO-only commands fetch no OpenID Connect
metadata first (commandRequiresAuthServer).

Upstream: not for upstream (a slicc build choice).
removeWhen: these commands can run on slicc.

